WEBVTT

00:00:07.708 --> 00:00:11.750
I don't know if it's even possible,

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:17.625
but I want to find a way
to save Koro Sensei's life.

00:00:17.625 --> 00:00:19.417
Save it?

00:00:19.417 --> 00:00:24.167
You mean, a way to keep Koro Sensei
from exploding come March?

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:25.875
Where do we start?

00:00:25.875 --> 00:00:28.375
I don't know yet.

00:00:28.375 --> 00:00:30.292
I don't know, but...

00:00:30.292 --> 00:00:32.125
I'm in!

00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:36.292
I wanna look for tons more
creepy-crawlies with Koro Sensei!

00:00:36.292 --> 00:00:37.583
Kurahashi...

00:00:37.583 --> 00:00:41.542
If you hadn't said something,
Nagisa, I would have.

00:00:41.542 --> 00:00:43.500
I want to repay him.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.833
Kataoka...

00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:48.000
Our assassination work
has gotten us far enough.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.458
Let's tackle a whole new challenge!

00:00:51.458 --> 00:00:53.792
Like launching a new series!

00:00:53.792 --> 00:00:55.750
We'll regret it if we don't.

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:59.208
We should do what we can, at least.

00:00:59.208 --> 00:01:01.208
You guys...

00:01:01.208 --> 00:01:02.792
Thank goodness.

00:01:02.792 --> 00:01:04.958
I'm glad they feel the same way.

00:01:04.958 --> 00:01:06.917
Amen to that, Okano!

00:01:07.375 --> 00:01:11.458
I hate to spoil the mood...

00:01:11.458 --> 00:01:12.792
...but I'm against the idea.

00:01:12.792 --> 00:01:14.333
Huh?

00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:19.625
Our bond is one of assassin and target.
Koro Sensei said as much.

00:01:19.625 --> 00:01:25.750
And I really treasure the bond
we've built over this past year.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.625
But that's exactly why...

00:01:27.625 --> 00:01:30.625
...I think we have to kill him.

00:01:30.625 --> 00:01:33.333
Nakamura...

00:01:39.375 --> 00:01:41.792
<i>"Wait, just hang on a sec!"</i>

00:01:41.792 --> 00:01:44.792
<i>I scream, but it gets me nowhere</i>

00:01:44.792 --> 00:01:47.250
<i>I put all my strength into being afraid of</i>

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.042
<i>The limits that just kept on closing in</i>

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:52.625
<i>Reality is merciless</i>

00:01:52.625 --> 00:01:55.333
<i>And time is especially tricky</i>

00:01:55.333 --> 00:02:00.583
<i>It's like someone's snatching away</i>
<i>the blanket I just can't sleep without</i>

00:02:00.583 --> 00:02:06.667
<i>We laughed and fretted</i>

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:11.208
<i>Over silly things, nonsensical things</i>

00:02:11.208 --> 00:02:17.333
<i>Once the final bell rings out</i>

00:02:17.333 --> 00:02:21.917
<i>The fun times will be over, too</i>

00:02:21.917 --> 00:02:23.458
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:02:23.458 --> 00:02:29.458
<i>365 days' worth of lessons shoved into bags</i>

00:02:29.458 --> 00:02:32.542
<i>Like always, like it's "see you tomorrow"</i>

00:02:32.542 --> 00:02:34.125
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:02:34.125 --> 00:02:38.208
<i>365 days' worth of happenings</i>

00:02:38.208 --> 00:02:43.208
<i>If you've made me an adult,</i>
<i>don't be showing me tears</i>

00:02:43.208 --> 00:02:44.708
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:02:44.708 --> 00:02:48.792
<i>365 days' worth of memories</i>

00:02:48.792 --> 00:02:51.292
<i>Even if I grow up some more</i>

00:02:51.292 --> 00:02:54.125
<i>They still won't fade a bit</i>

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:08.000
"17th Period: Discord Time"
"by Taisei Yoshida"

00:03:08.458 --> 00:03:09.875
You're against it?

00:03:09.875 --> 00:03:13.667
You say you wanna save him,
but <i>how</i>, exactly?

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:14.708
B-But--

00:03:14.708 --> 00:03:17.417
It's not like we haven't thought about it.

00:03:17.417 --> 00:03:22.917
But... what if time runs out
before we find a way?

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:26.458
You think that octopus'll be happy,
havin' such half-assed students,

00:03:26.458 --> 00:03:29.583
comin' to such a half-assed ending?

00:03:30.333 --> 00:03:32.667
--B-But isn't it at least worth consid--

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:35.292
--It's always the talented ones,
--B-But isn't it at least worth consid--

00:03:35.292 --> 00:03:40.167
mistakenly thinking everything'll go their way.

00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:44.583
Hey, Nagisa, aren't you getting
a tad full of yourself?

00:03:44.583 --> 00:03:45.625
Huh?

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:49.875
Here you are, the most
gifted assassin in the E Class,

00:03:49.875 --> 00:03:53.417
and you're suggesting we just
quit this assassination?

00:03:53.417 --> 00:03:55.125
What about the talentless students

00:03:55.125 --> 00:03:59.083
who've still been trying
their hardest to kill him?

00:03:59.083 --> 00:04:00.875
To put it another way,

00:04:00.875 --> 00:04:03.417
it's like a hot woman
telling a bunch of homely ones

00:04:03.417 --> 00:04:08.708
they should all quit trying
so hard to find boyfriends.

00:04:08.708 --> 00:04:11.875
Th-That's not what I...

00:04:11.875 --> 00:04:16.792
Besides, when it comes to assassination,
you're way better than me.

00:04:16.792 --> 00:04:20.250
You saying that just ticks me off even more.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:23.708
Isn't it more like you're
the worst at understanding

00:04:23.708 --> 00:04:25.625
how the less powerful feel?

00:04:25.625 --> 00:04:28.083
No! That's not it!

00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:30.125
I'm being honest with my feelings!

00:04:30.125 --> 00:04:33.042
Do you hate Koro Sensei?

00:04:33.042 --> 00:04:36.333
We saw that movie with him...
and had all kinds of fun!

00:04:36.333 --> 00:04:37.583
That's just it!

00:04:37.583 --> 00:04:41.042
That octopus put everything he had
into making a fun classroom

00:04:41.042 --> 00:04:43.625
that <i>wouldn't </i>turn out lazy losers like you!

00:04:43.625 --> 00:04:48.083
This classroom couldn't exist
if our bloodlust were blunted!

00:04:48.083 --> 00:04:50.500
Can't you see all his hard work?

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:54.542
Or do you have
little-kid brains to match your body?

00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:57.083
Oh?

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:03.125
Huh? What's with that look?

00:05:03.125 --> 00:05:08.333
An itty-bitty mouse like you, defying a human?

00:05:08.333 --> 00:05:09.792
I just...

00:05:09.792 --> 00:05:11.667
Got something to say?

00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:14.833
How about you say it after
beating me in a fight for once?

00:05:14.833 --> 00:05:17.000
I'll gladly take you on. Bring it.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:20.167
C'mon. C'mon! C'mon!

00:05:27.708 --> 00:05:30.250
A-A flying triangle choke!

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:32.083
I...

00:05:32.083 --> 00:05:34.250
...am <i>not </i>going off half-assed!

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.042
When did Nagisa learn <i>that</i>?

00:05:37.042 --> 00:05:38.500
Still...

00:05:39.875 --> 00:05:43.042
...he's no match for Karma in combat!

00:05:44.125 --> 00:05:45.667
Why, you...

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:47.333
Stop that!

00:05:47.333 --> 00:05:49.333
What the hell are you two trying to prove?!

00:05:49.333 --> 00:05:53.167
Urgh! This guy is crazy strong...!

00:05:55.583 --> 00:05:59.125
Dammit! Chill out already!

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:02.542
A junior-high fight? Most excellent!

00:06:02.542 --> 00:06:06.750
But this classroom is based in assassination--

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:10.042
shouldn't you decide things with <i>these</i>?

00:06:11.583 --> 00:06:14.750
Now the instigator's trying to mediate?!

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.458
"Blue" "Red"

00:06:16.917 --> 00:06:19.167
Red and blue paintballs?

00:06:19.167 --> 00:06:22.167
"Red"
Red for those who want to kill me,

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:24.125
"Blue"
blue for those who don't.

00:06:24.125 --> 00:06:24.792
blue for those who don't.

00:06:24.792 --> 00:06:29.708
First, everyone will state his or her
position clearly and choose a color.

00:06:29.708 --> 00:06:32.917
Then you'll do battle here on this mountain.

00:06:32.917 --> 00:06:37.208
The class will accept
the opinion of the winning team.

00:06:37.958 --> 00:06:40.583
Win or lose, no grudges allowed!

00:06:40.583 --> 00:06:42.417
What do you say?

00:06:44.167 --> 00:06:45.417
You know,

00:06:45.417 --> 00:06:46.125
"Blue" "Red"

00:06:46.125 --> 00:06:49.208
"Blue" "Red"
I'll respect your decision, my dear students,

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:51.375
"Blue" "Red"
if you give your all to reach it.

00:06:51.375 --> 00:06:57.500
What I'd hate most is
for this class to end in discord.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:03.292
If you care about me...
just promise me that won't happen.

00:07:03.292 --> 00:07:06.542
"Blue" "Red"

00:07:06.542 --> 00:07:07.958
"Blue" "Red"
Well?

00:07:11.167 --> 00:07:11.542
"Blue" "Red"

00:07:11.542 --> 00:07:14.000
"Blue" "Red"
All right, we'll settle it with these:

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:15.333
All right, we'll settle it with these:

00:07:15.333 --> 00:07:17.875
kill

00:07:17.875 --> 00:07:19.792
or don't kill.

00:07:23.542 --> 00:07:27.375
Okay. I guess I'll choose.

00:07:27.375 --> 00:07:29.083
Me, too.

00:07:29.083 --> 00:07:32.125
Working so hard toward that insta-kill shot...

00:07:32.125 --> 00:07:34.667
I think we've come a long way.

00:07:34.667 --> 00:07:38.417
As for who--or what--brought us this far?

00:07:38.417 --> 00:07:41.292
"Red"
We don't want to take our eyes off that target.

00:07:41.292 --> 00:07:42.583
"Red"
And so...

00:07:42.583 --> 00:07:44.625
...we want to keep going.

00:07:44.625 --> 00:07:46.083
"Ryunosuke Chiba, Rinka Hayami: 'Kill'"

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.917
Chiba... Hayami...

00:07:48.917 --> 00:07:54.917
When I tried to kill
Koro Sensei? I regretted it.

00:07:54.917 --> 00:07:58.958
I wanted him to live longer.

00:07:58.958 --> 00:08:01.125
It must run in the family--

00:08:01.125 --> 00:08:04.333
"Blue"
my sister must've thought the same way.

00:08:04.333 --> 00:08:05.875
"Blue"
And that's why I...

00:08:05.875 --> 00:08:06.917
And that's why I...

00:08:06.917 --> 00:08:08.875
I want to keep Koro Sensei safe.

00:08:08.875 --> 00:08:10.375
"Kaede Kayano: 'Don't Kill'"

00:08:11.792 --> 00:08:14.958
Does having a thing for assassins
run in the family, too?

00:08:14.958 --> 00:08:17.042
The power of science is infinite!

00:08:17.042 --> 00:08:21.083
If it can destroy,
then surely it can protect, too!

00:08:21.083 --> 00:08:24.208
Besides, it's not like there's no hope at all.

00:08:24.208 --> 00:08:27.292
If we all come together,
we can see for ourselves.

00:08:27.292 --> 00:08:28.750
"Kotaro Takebayashi, Manami Okuda:
'Don't Kill'"

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:35.167
Us hands-on types see the assassination
itself as our graduation project.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.417
If Koro Sensei's gonna die when time runs out,

00:08:39.417 --> 00:08:42.542
we'd sooner show him our finest masterpiece.

00:08:42.542 --> 00:08:44.042
"Taiga Okajima, Sosuke Sugaya,
Koki Mimura: 'Kill'"

00:08:44.542 --> 00:08:46.625
Koro Sensei's the one who told me

00:08:46.625 --> 00:08:49.542
to be an assassin
worthy of the name "Justice."

00:08:49.542 --> 00:08:52.250
I'll take that advice.

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.750
"Masayoshi Kimura: 'Kill'"

00:08:54.125 --> 00:08:59.000
I'd like him to keep giving us <i>more </i>advice.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.458
"Yukiko Kanzaki: 'Don't Kill'"

00:09:00.583 --> 00:09:04.042
The planet's life or our teacher's life?

00:09:04.042 --> 00:09:07.958
You could weigh the two
until the cows come home.

00:09:07.958 --> 00:09:10.458
Let's cut the crap and kill him.

00:09:10.458 --> 00:09:11.833
"Kirara Hazama: 'Kill'"

00:09:11.833 --> 00:09:17.917
I want to be true to my own feelings.
Isn't that enough?

00:09:17.917 --> 00:09:19.375
"Toka Yada: 'Don't Kill'"

00:09:19.542 --> 00:09:21.500
Of course it is!

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:23.958
Me and him, we're simple guys at heart:

00:09:23.958 --> 00:09:27.458
we want to save him because
we want to save him! Right?

00:09:27.458 --> 00:09:31.625
Yeah, though I do want to
respect everyone else's opinions.

00:09:31.625 --> 00:09:33.208
"Yuma Isogai, Hiroto Maehara: 'Don't Kill'"

00:09:33.208 --> 00:09:37.833
"Red"
I'm simple, too. I joined this class to kill him.

00:09:37.833 --> 00:09:42.125
In coming to kill him, I met you guys.

00:09:42.125 --> 00:09:44.708
It's fun, spending our days
trying to kill Koro Sensei.

00:09:44.708 --> 00:09:47.583
And that's reason enough for me.

00:09:47.583 --> 00:09:49.000
"Itona Horibe: 'Kill'"

00:09:49.125 --> 00:09:54.708
Killing Koro Sensei may be my prime directive,

00:09:54.708 --> 00:09:57.542
but after many repeated thoughts and actions,

00:09:57.542 --> 00:10:00.250
I've come to recognize that the target's death

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:04.292
would be our greatest loss.

00:10:04.292 --> 00:10:10.458
It's difficult to determine the correct
decision with my current specs.

00:10:10.458 --> 00:10:13.292
In the spirit of cooperation,
I will remain neutral.

00:10:13.292 --> 00:10:14.708
"Autonomous Intelligence Fixed Artillery:
Neutral"

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:19.292
I <i>was </i>in the don't-kill camp...

00:10:19.292 --> 00:10:23.375
...but after hearing everyone's
thoughts, I'm not so sure.

00:10:23.375 --> 00:10:29.250
Koro Sensei, killing you
doesn't mean we hate you, right?

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:31.750
Of course not, Okano.

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:36.958
In fact, when I'm being killed
is when I feel closest to you all.

00:10:36.958 --> 00:10:40.375
In that case... Sorry, Nagisa.

00:10:40.375 --> 00:10:43.792
I think my feelings
are closer to these guys' here.

00:10:43.792 --> 00:10:45.250
"Hinata Okano: 'Kill'"

00:10:45.667 --> 00:10:47.917
Uh-huh...

00:10:47.917 --> 00:10:52.292
I'm ashamed to have been
so full of my own opinions.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.917
"Nagisa Shiota: 'Don't Kill'"

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:00.708
"Karma Akabane: 'Kill'"

00:11:01.125 --> 00:11:02.208
Hmph!

00:11:02.208 --> 00:11:04.000
"Blue" "Red"

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:07.917
Aw, man... they're totally fighting, all right.

00:11:07.917 --> 00:11:09.833
"Tomohito Sugino: 'Don't Kill'"

00:11:09.833 --> 00:11:12.417
You know, I've been wondering...

00:11:12.417 --> 00:11:13.125
Hmm?

00:11:13.125 --> 00:11:16.833
Those two have been friends
a long time, right?

00:11:16.833 --> 00:11:22.083
Yeah, they've been classmates since
our first year, and they hang out a lot.

00:11:22.083 --> 00:11:23.833
Well, for all that...

00:11:23.833 --> 00:11:26.750
...there's still this space between them.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:30.708
It's like they treat each other
like guests or something.

00:11:30.708 --> 00:11:33.750
Even the way they talk to each other...

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:34.458
"Blue" "Red"

00:11:34.458 --> 00:11:38.167
"Blue" "Red"
Okay--we've all picked sides.

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:48.000
"Assassination Classroom, Final Season"
"by Karma Akabane"

00:11:49.542 --> 00:11:54.375
Steal the other team's flag
or wipe them out to win.

00:11:54.375 --> 00:11:56.833
I'll be the referee.

00:11:56.833 --> 00:12:01.708
I'll make calls and watch for zombies
and other illegal plays from the midpoint.

00:12:01.708 --> 00:12:05.958
Otherwise, I'll pretend I don't know
where you're attacking from,

00:12:05.958 --> 00:12:07.958
so don't worry.

00:12:07.958 --> 00:12:10.708
Even if they stick with
the assassination, doubts and all,

00:12:10.708 --> 00:12:13.458
I know they won't succeed.

00:12:13.458 --> 00:12:19.167
It's one big gamble whether the class
can even focus on assassination again.

00:12:20.083 --> 00:12:25.750
All right: let the intraclass
assassination survival game...

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:27.167
...begin!

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:31.167
"Blue: Kotaro Takebayashi" "Blue: Meg Kataoka" "Dead"
Dead at the gate?!

00:12:31.167 --> 00:12:35.208
Damn... spotted us just as
we were getting into position!

00:12:35.208 --> 00:12:39.875
Even though a BB's arc
goes off course after 50 meters...

00:12:39.875 --> 00:12:43.958
Fear Chiba's and Hayami's
super-long-distance snipe!

00:12:43.958 --> 00:12:45.333
Whoa...

00:12:45.333 --> 00:12:48.083
You've brought them up
to be monumental killers.

00:12:48.083 --> 00:12:52.125
Yes--and not just those two, either.

00:12:52.125 --> 00:12:54.792
You keep on aiming, Chiba...

00:12:54.792 --> 00:12:56.208
--Ack!
--Whoa!

00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:58.667
"Red: Taiga Okajima" "Red: Ryunosuke Chiba" "Dead"

00:12:58.667 --> 00:13:01.708
"Red: Taiga Okajima" "Red: Ryunosuke Chiba" "Dead"
No way... I had no idea--none!

00:13:01.708 --> 00:13:03.167
"Red: Taiga Okajima" "Red: Ryunosuke Chiba" "Dead"
I'd forgotten...

00:13:03.167 --> 00:13:07.000
Kanzaki's an ace at this online war game.

00:13:09.375 --> 00:13:13.000
I started playing to help in assassination
and eventually mastered it.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:14.875
I'm glad I did.

00:13:14.875 --> 00:13:17.000
It comes in handy for helping people.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.375
"Red: Sosuke Sugaya"
"Dead"

00:13:18.375 --> 00:13:21.375
Yukiko... She's sure been hiding
her light under a bushel.

00:13:21.375 --> 00:13:25.667
Yes, and she has a truly proper battle style.

00:13:25.667 --> 00:13:29.542
A frontal breakthrough
on this field is extremely difficult,

00:13:29.542 --> 00:13:33.917
so normally you'd circle around
from the outside and attack.

00:13:33.917 --> 00:13:35.708
However...

00:13:37.958 --> 00:13:43.500
That's right--you trained on
a virtual battlefield, didn't you.

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:47.708
But if you're coming after
one of our key positions,

00:13:47.708 --> 00:13:51.625
all I need to do is lie in wait
for you along the way.

00:13:55.625 --> 00:13:56.875
"Blue: Yukiko Kanzaki"
"Dead"

00:13:57.292 --> 00:14:01.250
Come in, red team. I'll take the lead.

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:06.000
Mimura, see that high point
to Mr. Karasuma's right?

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:08.042
Head there.

00:14:08.042 --> 00:14:09.167
Okay!

00:14:09.167 --> 00:14:11.333
Don't let anyone see you.

00:14:11.333 --> 00:14:15.500
Terasaka, you and the other two stooges
are on defense at Face Rock.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:18.125
It'll be big trouble if they
make it past there, so play it tight.

00:14:18.125 --> 00:14:19.583
Gettin' used again, huh?

00:14:19.583 --> 00:14:21.750
Shut it!

00:14:22.167 --> 00:14:24.667
Ah, well done out there.

00:14:24.667 --> 00:14:28.833
How careless, to be killed right at the start.

00:14:28.833 --> 00:14:31.667
It was probably on Karma's orders.

00:14:31.667 --> 00:14:32.958
So all this time...

00:14:32.958 --> 00:14:38.083
...that red-headed kid's
had the most up his sleeve?

00:14:39.583 --> 00:14:41.667
Karma! I'm in position!

00:14:41.667 --> 00:14:45.542
Okay. You should see the enemies'
positions pretty well from there.

00:14:45.542 --> 00:14:48.833
I'll give orders to the team
once you report on those.

00:14:48.833 --> 00:14:52.875
Mimura's unassuming looks
are perfect for covert ops,

00:14:52.875 --> 00:14:55.917
plus his producer's eye
makes for a wide field of view.

00:14:55.917 --> 00:14:58.833
Hence his knack for reconnaissance in force--

00:14:58.833 --> 00:15:01.250
--not that anyone in our class ever noticed.

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:03.000
--Sugino and Fuwa, I think, in the forest on the right flank.
--not that anyone in our class ever noticed.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.833
--Sugino and Fuwa, I think, in the forest on the right flank.

00:15:04.833 --> 00:15:09.958
Nice, Mimura. Next up, Hazama. Advance.

00:15:14.667 --> 00:15:15.500
"Blue: Tomohito Sugino" "Blue: Yuzuki Fuwa" "Dead"

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:21.042
"Blue: Tomohito Sugino" "Blue: Yuzuki Fuwa" "Dead"
Where'd Hazama come from?!

00:15:21.042 --> 00:15:23.250
Use <i>me </i>as a sacrifice, will you?

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:24.792
I'll be cursing <i>you </i>later, Karma.

00:15:24.792 --> 00:15:26.167
"Red: Kirara Hazama" "Dead"
I'll be cursing <i>you </i>later, Karma.

00:15:26.417 --> 00:15:29.583
Muscling the slim Hazama in there like that...

00:15:29.583 --> 00:15:32.750
Karma must have expected
a simultaneous strike.

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:37.333
Yeah... but Hazama sucks at fighting,
and she took down two--

00:15:37.333 --> 00:15:41.292
one of them Sugino,
the close-combat superstar.

00:15:41.292 --> 00:15:45.750
We need a surprise attack
when the enemy's ranks are in shambles.

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:46.458
Okano?

00:15:46.458 --> 00:15:48.042
On it!

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:51.792
"Blue: Hinano Kurahashi" "Dead"
Huh?

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:54.000
Hinano!

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:57.500
I lost the Battle of the Hinas!

00:15:59.333 --> 00:16:03.042
Nicely done, Kayano! Holding out on us, huh?

00:16:03.042 --> 00:16:06.042
Where were those moves in gym class?!

00:16:06.042 --> 00:16:09.542
I trained plenty for my acting job.

00:16:09.542 --> 00:16:12.208
Now, without the pain of those tentacles,

00:16:12.208 --> 00:16:14.167
I can actually focus!

00:16:14.167 --> 00:16:15.875
Rats!

00:16:16.333 --> 00:16:19.500
I'll keep Koro Sensei safe!

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:27.250
Wish we'd seen this earnest side
of you sooner, Kayano.

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:29.750
While you were working hard on your own,

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:33.167
we were all polishing up the
for-realsies parts of ourselves, too.

00:16:33.167 --> 00:16:37.042
Whatever we end up doing
because of this battle,

00:16:37.042 --> 00:16:41.083
<i>this </i>time we're all being earnest together.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.292
Okie-doke! Later!

00:16:43.292 --> 00:16:46.583
Oh--remind me to get your autograph!

00:16:48.292 --> 00:16:50.000
"Blue: Kaede Kayano"
"Dead"

00:16:50.208 --> 00:16:53.917
All right! Let's keep this up
and take down another couple-three!

00:16:53.917 --> 00:16:57.125
Huh? But Karma said to hit and run!

00:16:57.125 --> 00:16:58.417
Check that out:

00:16:58.417 --> 00:17:01.125
It's Hara, and she's wide open!

00:17:01.125 --> 00:17:03.875
Tonight's rations, here I come!

00:17:04.958 --> 00:17:09.125
A homemade trap I worked on
at night. Mama's mighty!

00:17:09.125 --> 00:17:12.750
The unarmed Hara must have
looked like some tasty prey.

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:14.708
Can't do a thing now, can you?

00:17:14.708 --> 00:17:14.833
Hey, no butt-cutting!

00:17:14.833 --> 00:17:16.833
"Red: Hinata Okano" "Red: Masayoshi Kimura" "Dead"
Hey, no butt-cutting!

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:19.333
He got ahead of himself.

00:17:19.333 --> 00:17:22.500
Why can't people just do as they're told?

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:27.125
Ah, well. Should your lieutenant
finish things off, then?

00:17:27.125 --> 00:17:29.042
I can use the stooges, right?

00:17:29.042 --> 00:17:32.917
You know me so well. Much obliged.

00:17:33.833 --> 00:17:35.750
Oh! Over there!

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:40.833
I <i>thought </i>our formation had been leaked,
and sure enough--they see us!

00:17:40.833 --> 00:17:41.250
"Red: Koki Mimura" "Dead"

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:44.250
"Red: Koki Mimura" "Dead"
Both sides are down to half their strength.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:48.292
Time to think about flag-capturing tactics.

00:17:48.292 --> 00:17:48.750
"Blue: Sumire Hara" "Dead"
Time to think about flag-capturing tactics.

00:17:49.083 --> 00:17:51.250
I've been putting all my strategies into play

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:51.542
"Survivor Count"
I've been putting all my strategies into play

00:17:51.542 --> 00:17:54.500
"Survivor Count"
knowing it would come to this.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:57.250
"Survivor Count"
We took down Kataoka and Takebayashi

00:17:57.250 --> 00:18:00.583
"Survivor Count"
to rob the enemy of strategic options.

00:18:00.583 --> 00:18:07.417
That's why I have Hayami
posted at our most crucial spot.

00:18:07.417 --> 00:18:10.583
Guard it right, now, Itona.

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:14.167
Whoa!

00:18:14.167 --> 00:18:15.000
Tch!

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:17.875
Chiba can shoot farther
and hits the target more often,

00:18:17.875 --> 00:18:21.542
but her kinetic vision and
sense of balance are miles better.

00:18:21.542 --> 00:18:25.917
An active battlefield like this
is where she really shines.

00:18:26.625 --> 00:18:28.667
That Hayami is bad news!

00:18:28.667 --> 00:18:30.667
Gotta approach carefully...

00:18:30.667 --> 00:18:31.542
"Isogai"
Even if we attack from the opposite side,

00:18:31.542 --> 00:18:33.125
"Terasaka"
Even if we attack from the opposite side,

00:18:33.125 --> 00:18:36.958
we'll have to break through Terasaka's solid defenses,

00:18:36.958 --> 00:18:38.042
<i>and </i>the area around the flag is within Hayami's range!

00:18:38.042 --> 00:18:41.292
"Hayami"
<i>and </i>the area around the flag is within Hayami's range!

00:18:41.292 --> 00:18:44.042
We'll have to take Hayami out first!

00:18:44.042 --> 00:18:48.167
Hayami, Itona. They'll be
coming in droves soon enough.

00:18:48.167 --> 00:18:51.792
Slow them down, at least.
And if you can, eliminate them.

00:18:51.792 --> 00:18:53.000
Roger.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:57.208
Nakamura, once the firefight starts,
you step in and finish it.

00:18:57.208 --> 00:18:58.417
Gotcha.

00:18:58.417 --> 00:19:00.375
I'm counting on you, meat wall!

00:19:00.375 --> 00:19:01.125
Say what?!

00:19:01.125 --> 00:19:06.750
While they're scuffling with Rinka,
I'll rush in with you as my shield.

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:11.833
Once you three are dead, I'll have
plenty of time to get to the flag.

00:19:11.833 --> 00:19:16.042
So you're sacrificing us?
Geez, you'll stop at nothing!

00:19:16.042 --> 00:19:17.875
Well, duh!

00:19:17.875 --> 00:19:24.125
I want to win this battle properly
and kill Koro Sensei as a class!

00:19:26.833 --> 00:19:32.375
Nakamura, you wanted to be
a dummy, so you did dumb stuff,

00:19:32.375 --> 00:19:37.083
and joined the "kill" camp first outta
some sense of duty to protect our bond.

00:19:37.083 --> 00:19:41.917
Y'know, you might be the most
no-nonsense one outta all of us.

00:19:41.917 --> 00:19:43.875
Hmph.

00:19:43.875 --> 00:19:48.875
The plan's as ready as it'll ever be.
The only disconcerting thing...

00:19:48.875 --> 00:19:52.792
...would be Nagisa,
who even Mimura couldn't find.

00:19:52.792 --> 00:19:55.292
Okay, guys, forget about defense.

00:19:55.292 --> 00:19:57.667
We go after Hayami and Itona
with everything we've got.

00:19:57.667 --> 00:20:01.208
If we kill those two, Karma'll be
the only one guarding the flag!

00:20:01.208 --> 00:20:03.458
Let's settle this once and for all!

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:07.583
Now. We're going in, too!

00:20:07.958 --> 00:20:09.375
Hah!

00:20:09.833 --> 00:20:10.500
"Blue: Manami Okuda" "Dead"

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:11.958
"Blue: Manami Okuda" "Dead"
Surround them from the left!

00:20:11.958 --> 00:20:12.917
Surround them from the left!

00:20:12.917 --> 00:20:17.542
Isogai's in the lead? If I can just
take him down, this is as good as won!

00:20:18.042 --> 00:20:19.500
"Blue: Yuma Isogai"
"Dead"

00:20:19.708 --> 00:20:26.042
I hate conflict, and I've never once
shot better than Rinka.

00:20:26.042 --> 00:20:29.625
But just this one shot--for Koro Sensei!

00:20:31.458 --> 00:20:31.833
"Red: Rinka Hayami" "Dead"

00:20:31.833 --> 00:20:33.333
"Red: Rinka Hayami" "Dead"
Yada...?

00:20:33.333 --> 00:20:34.667
I got her!

00:20:34.667 --> 00:20:35.542
And I got got...

00:20:35.542 --> 00:20:36.500
"Blue: Toka Yada"
"Dead"

00:20:40.542 --> 00:20:43.250
"Red: Itona Horibe"
"Dead"

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:46.083
I knew I was more of a knife guy...

00:20:46.083 --> 00:20:49.000
No way can I hit you guys with a gun.

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:51.083
Damn! They got you?!

00:20:51.083 --> 00:20:54.167
Doesn't matter: now the flag's underguarded.

00:20:54.167 --> 00:20:56.417
Nakamura--go get it.

00:20:56.417 --> 00:20:58.417
You bet!

00:21:06.583 --> 00:21:09.500
A-A back attack at point-blank range?

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:12.542
It came so suddenly--and out of nowhere!

00:21:12.542 --> 00:21:15.125
There wasn't anyone there until just now!

00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:44.750
<i>In the big window where</i>
<i>the dappled sunlight shines gently in</i>

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:56.708
<i>The day I met you felt so far away</i>

00:21:56.708 --> 00:22:07.667
<i>The memories I've arranged</i>
<i>little by little keep me warm</i>

00:22:07.667 --> 00:22:19.208
<i>A small room, hearts connecting:</i>
<i>you taught me gently</i>

00:22:19.208 --> 00:22:31.958
<i>Once this season comes for me, I won't be able</i>

00:22:31.958 --> 00:22:37.208
<i>To search out your figure anymore</i>

00:22:37.208 --> 00:22:42.958
<i>I'll never forget</i>

00:22:42.958 --> 00:23:02.102
<i>Until the day I can see you again</i>
